            </StoryText>
        </PageObject>
        <PageObject XPosition="752" YPosition="3826.0652173913" OwnPage="8" ItemID="946463453" ItemType="4" Width="266" Height="273.934782608696" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="9" LineColor="Black" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="1" ImageScaleY="1" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="1" ImageRatio="1" Columns="1" ColumnGap="0" AutomaticTextFrame="0" TextToFrameDistanceLeft="0" TextToFrameDistanceTop="0" TextToFrameDistanceBottom="0" TextToFrameDistanceRight="0" VerticalAlignment="0" FirstLineOffset="1" PathTextShowPath="0" PathTextDistanceFromPath="0" TextPathType="0" TextPathFlipped="0" Path="M0 0 L266 0 L266 273.935 L0 273.935 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L266 0 L266 273.935 L0 273.935 L0 0 Z" gXpos="140" gYpos="2162.06521739131" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <Content Font="Bebas Neue Regular" FontSize="24" Chars="Backstory"/>
                <para Parent="Header 1"/>
                <Content Chars="Zephir is an actor. They work primarily as a company player in a local children’s theatre but have also acted in more traditional plays. They believe that the most important truths can only be told through fiction. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="They are pansexual and currently unpartnered. They were previously in a relationship with Rin, which ended due to differing needs. They remain friends with Rin, but the relationship has not gotten back to where it was previously. They feel like they are on the edges of the friend group following the dissolution of the relationship. "/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PageObject>
        <PageObject XPosition="1074.60886267049" YPosition="3826.0652173913" OwnPage="8" ItemID="364157682" ItemType="4" Width="208.521739130435" Height="273.934782608696" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="9" LineColor="Black" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="1" ImageScaleY="1" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="1" ImageRatio="1" Columns="1" ColumnGap="0" AutomaticTextFrame="0" TextToFrameDistanceLeft="0" TextToFrameDistanceTop="0" TextToFrameDistanceBottom="0" TextToFrameDistanceRight="0" VerticalAlignment="0" FirstLineOffset="1" PathTextShowPath="0" PathTextDistanceFromPath="0" TextPathType="0" TextPathFlipped="0" Path="M0 0 L208.522 0 L208.522 273.935 L0 273.935 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L208.522 0 L208.522 273.935 L0 273.935 L0 0 Z" gXpos="462.608862670487" gYpos="2162.06521739131" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <Content Font="Bebas Neue Regular" FontSize="24" Chars="SPECIAL ABILITIES"/>
                <para Parent="Header 2"/>
                <Content Chars="Hide"/>
                <para Parent="Header 3"/>
                <Content Chars="Decreased likelihood of being targeted; changes to Surprise Attack while in effect"/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="Surprise Attack"/>
                <para Parent="Header 3"/>
                <Content Chars="Inflict a status debuff on the enemy  based on weapon mode. Dagger: Stun, Gun: Slow"/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="Weapon Mode"/>
                <para Parent="Header 3"/>
                <Content Chars="Changes primary weapon mode between dagger and gun"/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PageObject>
        <PageObject XPosition="140" YPosition="4220" OwnPage="9" ItemID="1754655207" ItemType="4" Width="532" Height="356" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="1" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="1" ImageScaleY="1" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="1" ImageRatio="1" Columns="1" ColumnGap="0" AutomaticTextFrame="0" TextToFrameDistanceLeft="0" TextToFrameDistanceTop="0" TextToFrameDistanceBottom="0" TextToFrameDistanceRight="0" VerticalAlignment="0" FirstLineOffset="1" PathTextShowPath="0" PathTextDistanceFromPath="0" TextPathType="0" TextPathFlipped="0" Path="M0 0 L532 0 L532 356 L0 356 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L532 0 L532 356 L0 356 L0 0 Z" gXpos="140" gYpos="4220" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <Content Chars="Sample Levels"/>
                <para Parent="Header 1"/>
                <Content Chars="The Hook: An Ordinary Night Out"/>
                <para Parent="Header 2"/>
                <Content Chars="As the game begins, a group of six friends are exploring a park inside a moderately sized city. Players can travel around the park and explore its various features, such as the pond, the dog park, and the playground. When they approach the playground, a loud crash is heard from the nearby woods, which begins the level’s primary objective: investigating the disturbance. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="Following the sound takes the player to a small walking path that eventually leads to a meteor crash site. There are small fires around, showing that it recently crashed and leading our players to believe (correctly) that this was the source of the noise. When the players get close to the meteor, it cracks open, and six slug-like creatures shoot out, one going to each character. The characters panic but are unable to react before the slugs disappear into their skin directly atop their spines. This event serves as the catalyst that provides players’ powers and is an indirect introduction to the biocomputers that support the cast of protagonist characters. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="Player Experience "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="The player’s emotional journey through this level takes them from comfort to curiosity to wonder. The characters are comfortable as the game starts, spending time with their long-time friends doing a routine thing. Players are given the opportunity to explore and bring curiosity to the world around them, which is punctuated by the sound of crashing that causes them to investigate. Then there is a sense of wonder as the players experience an event that is not yet explained but fantastical in nature. "/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PageObject>
        <PageObject XPosition="306.347826086957" YPosition="4576" OwnPage="9" ItemID="2069385893" ItemType="2" Width="199.304347826087" Height="356" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="1" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="0.184541062801932" ImageScaleY="0.184541062801932" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="0" ImageRatio="1" ImagePageNumber="0" ImageFileName="sammi_map_1.png" ImageProfile="Embedded sRGB built-in" ImageColorimetricIntent="0" EmbeddedProfile="Embedded sRGB built-in" Path="M0 0 L199.304 0 L199.304 356 L0 356 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L199.304 0 L199.304 356 L0 356 L0 0 Z" gXpos="306.347826086957" gYpos="4576" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1"/>
        <PageObject XPosition="752" YPosition="4220" OwnPage="10" ItemID="2147480635" ItemType="4" Width="532" Height="400.521739130436" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="1" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="1" ImageScaleY="1" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="1" ImageRatio="1" Columns="1" ColumnGap="0" AutomaticTextFrame="0" TextToFrameDistanceLeft="0" TextToFrameDistanceTop="0" TextToFrameDistanceBottom="0" TextToFrameDistanceRight="0" VerticalAlignment="0" FirstLineOffset="1" PathTextShowPath="0" PathTextDistanceFromPath="0" TextPathType="0" TextPathFlipped="0" Path="M0 0 L532 0 L532 400.522 L0 400.522 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L532 0 L532 400.522 L0 400.522 L0 0 Z" gXpos="752" gYpos="4220" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <Content Chars="Plot Point: First Combat "/>
                <para Parent="Header 2"/>
                <Content Chars="Between the opening level and the beginning of this level, players have discovered their powers and the biocomputers that are now permanently bonded to them but have not yet used their powers in any kind of combat scenario. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="The level begins with the players arriving at a local shopping area where a monster is attacking civilians. This is their first experience with the monstrous forces of the game, which causes them to hesitate. In their time of indecision, the monster smashes the fountain and injures innocent people, which drives the team to act. They rush in to fight the monster, winning easily. This level also serves as a combat tutorial, so the player is guided through the fight to ensure a relatively easy victory. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="After the fight, the team spends some time discussing the damage and devastation around them. Players can either leave immediately after this discussion or stay to help the injured and assist with cleanup. Staying will increase the public’s perception of the team, which will have mechanical benefits later in the game. Whether they leave immediately or stay to assist, the team eventually separates to think about the situation they find themselves in. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="Player Experience "/>
                <para Parent="Header 3"/>
                <Content Chars="Players begin this level with uncertainty, as they have not yet been given an opportunity to use their new powers. That uncertainty leads to urgency as the players are required to save civilians who are under threat and not prepared. The music will underscore this urgency. As the level teaches them how combat works, players will be empowered to complete the fight on their own with the knowledge they have been granted. Finally, the players are given the opportunity to feel responsibility by giving them the option to stay and help their community and being exposed to the Reputation system for the first time. "/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PageObject>
        <PageObject XPosition="907.887026210849" YPosition="4620.52173913044" OwnPage="10" ItemID="82754584" ItemType="2" Width="220.225947578303" Height="311.478260869564" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="1" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="0.277362654380734" ImageScaleY="0.277362654380734" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="0" ImageRatio="1" ImagePageNumber="0" ImageFileName="sammi_map_2.png" ImageColorimetricIntent="0" UseEmbeddedProfile="0" Path="M0 0 L220.226 0 L220.226 311.478 L0 311.478 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L220.226 0 L220.226 311.478 L0 311.478 L0 0 Z" gXpos="907.887026210849" gYpos="4620.52173913044" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1"/>
        <PageObject XPosition="140" YPosition="5052" OwnPage="11" ItemID="1733624296" ItemType="4" Width="532" Height="325.043478260871" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="1" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="1" ImageScaleY="1" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="1" ImageRatio="1" Columns="1" ColumnGap="0" AutomaticTextFrame="0" TextToFrameDistanceLeft="0" TextToFrameDistanceTop="0" TextToFrameDistanceBottom="0" TextToFrameDistanceRight="0" VerticalAlignment="0" FirstLineOffset="1" PathTextShowPath="0" PathTextDistanceFromPath="0" TextPathType="0" TextPathFlipped="0" Path="M0 0 L532 0 L532 325.043 L0 325.043 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L532 0 L532 325.043 L0 325.043 L0 0 Z" gXpos="140" gYpos="5052" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <Content Chars="Pinch Point: Introduction to the Villain "/>
                <para Parent="Header 2"/>
                <Content Chars="By this point, the team has been operating for a bit of time. Players have been able to explore and fight battles with monsters but do not know where they are coming from. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="This level begins with the team arriving at the Pier, discovering what they believe to be just another average monster attack. They engage with the monster as normal, but just before the monster is defeated, it is joined by a large, menacing creature. This creature is more intentional than the monsters they have faced previously, and they have never had to face more than one monster at a time (excluding mooks). This changes the flow of battle completely and turns what was nearly a victory into a crushing defeat. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="Following the battle, the newcomer introduces themselves as Vince O'Ruin. He mocks the team’s strength, remarking that they “don’t know why they were worried” and that they “won’t debase themselves further by killing such weaklings.” The team leaves, having suffered their first defeat and learning that there are much larger forces at play than they knew. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="Player Experience "/>
                <para Parent="Header 3"/>
                <Content Chars="By this point in the game, players should feel confident about their abilities. They have yet to be truly tested either in combat or in the narrative. That confidence turns into shock when they experience the main villain, Vince O’Ruin, for the first time. After their crushing defeat, they will feel somewhat helpless but determined to improve. "/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PageObject>
        <PageObject XPosition="268.260869565217" YPosition="5377.04347826087" OwnPage="11" ItemID="303036672" ItemType="2" Width="275.478260869565" Height="386.956521739129" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="1" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="0.344573928529946" ImageScaleY="0.344573928529946" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="0" ImageRatio="1" ImagePageNumber="0" ImageFileName="sammi_map_3.png" ImageColorimetricIntent="0" UseEmbeddedProfile="0" Path="M0 0 L275.478 0 L275.478 386.957 L0 386.957 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L275.478 0 L275.478 386.957 L0 386.957 L0 0 Z" gXpos="268.260869565217" gYpos="5377.04347826087" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1"/>
        <PageObject XPosition="752" YPosition="5052" OwnPage="12" ItemID="1786397079" ItemType="4" Width="532" Height="514.956521739132" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="1" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="1" ImageScaleY="1" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="1" ImageRatio="1" Columns="1" ColumnGap="0" AutomaticTextFrame="0" TextToFrameDistanceLeft="0" TextToFrameDistanceTop="0" TextToFrameDistanceBottom="0" TextToFrameDistanceRight="0" VerticalAlignment="0" FirstLineOffset="1" PathTextShowPath="0" PathTextDistanceFromPath="0" TextPathType="0" TextPathFlipped="0" Path="M0 0 L532 0 L532 514.957 L0 514.957 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L532 0 L532 514.957 L0 514.957 L0 0 Z" gXpos="752" gYpos="5052" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <Content Chars="Midpoint: Assault on Enemy Stronghold "/>
                <para Parent="Header 2"/>
                <Content Chars="After a series of battles with the monsters that are attacking the city, the team is tired of not making any progress on ending the threat for good. They know they can’t just react but need to find a way to be proactive about the conflict. With this goal, they put their efforts toward locating the villain’s base. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="They catch a lucky break when a monster steps out of a portal in front of them. Alpha, the biocomputer bonded to Rin, scans the monster and determines that the monsters are coming from a pocket dimension, which explains how they just appear without anyone seeing them beforehand. The data they gather is enough to recreate the dimensional frequency, which allows them to access the villain’s stronghold. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="The team is shocked to discover that the villain’s lair is not a ruined temple or an opulent castle, but is instead a standard, almost boring office building. They take the elevator to the floor where Vince O'Ruin’s office is located, and search for any information on the villain’s plans or how to stop him. They discover that the villain’s goal is to connect Earth to his company’s Head Office and strip it of resources. They also discover that he has done this to other planets, including the one the biocomputers came from. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="When the players are ready to leave, they discover a veritable army of mooks waiting for them in the lobby. No matter how hard the player fights, more enemies always appear, so it is impossible for them to fight their way out of the scenario. The only way to end it is to go through the gauntlet and escape through the portal. When the players finally make it through the portal, it closes behind them. This is when they discover that Zephir did not make it through the portal and was left behind. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="Player Experience "/>
                <para Parent="Header 3"/>
                <Content Chars="The determination from the players’ introduction to the villain may be waning by now, so the player is provided with an opportunity to assault their headquarters, effectively reigniting that determination. Once again, players are faced with an opportunity to explore an area, though this time it is with a goal in mind, so the curiosity is tempered but remains as a feeling of discovery. When players are ambushed on the way out, there is pressure, both literally from the press of enemies around them and emotionally from the need to escape. Once the team is through the gauntlet, players will experience loss with the surprise (presumably unwilling) departure of Zephir. "/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PageObject>
        <PageObject XPosition="878.603726708074" YPosition="5566.95652173913" OwnPage="12" ItemID="1802513906" ItemType="2" Width="278.792546583851" Height="197.043478260868" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="1" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="0.248165589749204" ImageScaleY="0.248165589749204" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="0" ImageRatio="1" ImagePageNumber="0" ImageFileName="sammi_map_4.png" ImageProfile="Embedded sRGB built-in" ImageColorimetricIntent="0" EmbeddedProfile="Embedded sRGB built-in" Path="M0 0 L278.793 0 L278.793 197.043 L0 197.043 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L278.793 0 L278.793 197.043 L0 197.043 L0 0 Z" gXpos="878.603726708074" gYpos="5566.95652173913" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1"/>
        <PageObject XPosition="140" YPosition="5884" OwnPage="13" ItemID="674650229" ItemType="4" Width="532" Height="415.478260869567" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="1" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="1" ImageScaleY="1" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="1" ImageRatio="1" Columns="1" ColumnGap="0" AutomaticTextFrame="0" TextToFrameDistanceLeft="0" TextToFrameDistanceTop="0" TextToFrameDistanceBottom="0" TextToFrameDistanceRight="0" VerticalAlignment="0" FirstLineOffset="1" PathTextShowPath="0" PathTextDistanceFromPath="0" TextPathType="0" TextPathFlipped="0" Path="M0 0 L532 0 L532 415.478 L0 415.478 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L532 0 L532 415.478 L0 415.478 L0 0 Z" gXpos="140" gYpos="5884" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <Content Chars="Pinch Point: Betrayal "/>
                <para Parent="Header 2"/>
                <Content Chars="Following the loss of Zephir, the team gathers in their unofficial sanctum, Morgan’s apartment/studio. They are discussing how they will rescue Zephir when the front door opens and they walk in. The team is overjoyed and celebrates, but it is cut short when they get word of a monster attack at a tech company’s offices downtown. The team gathers in the garage to head out, but Zephir attacks without warning. Zephir is significantly stronger than they had been and ends the fight quickly. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="Zephir monologues before leaving, saying that they are happy they don’t have to pretend to be friends with these weak, indecisive losers. They say that if they had waited on the team to rescue them, they would have died in that pocket dimension and they are glad they joined the winning team finally. They are particularly brutal to Rin, with whom they were previously in a romantic relationship. They also let slip that they couldn’t risk the team interrupting their attack on the tech company, so Zephir was sent to take them out of commission. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="After Zephir leaves, the team is disheartened and distraught. They have lost both a friend and a teammate, who is suddenly way more powerful than they are. Rin believes there is more to the story than just Zephir turning traitor but agrees that they need enough power to defend themselves and their community either way. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="Player Experience "/>
                <para Parent="Header 3"/>
                <Content Chars="Players begin this level feeling a mix of confusion, shock, and grief at the loss of a main character. When Zephir returns, they will experience immediate relief, but that is snatched away as Zephir assaults them. Following their defeat, players will once again feel helpless and vulnerable, unsure of how to move forward. They have been attacked in their own home by someone they thought was a friend, and the uncertainty that causes both players and characters should feel equally impactful. "/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PageObject>
        <PageObject XPosition="752" YPosition="5884" OwnPage="14" ItemID="1398940813" ItemType="4" Width="532" Height="473.913043478263" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="1" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="1" ImageScaleY="1" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="1" ImageRatio="1" Columns="1" ColumnGap="0" AutomaticTextFrame="0" TextToFrameDistanceLeft="0" TextToFrameDistanceTop="0" TextToFrameDistanceBottom="0" TextToFrameDistanceRight="0" VerticalAlignment="0" FirstLineOffset="1" PathTextShowPath="0" PathTextDistanceFromPath="0" TextPathType="0" TextPathFlipped="0" Path="M0 0 L532 0 L532 473.913 L0 473.913 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L532 0 L532 473.913 L0 473.913 L0 0 Z" gXpos="752" gYpos="5884" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <Content Chars="Plot Point: Visiting Synthax One "/>
                <para Parent="Header 2"/>
                <Content Chars="The biocomputers tell the team about a possible path to upgrading their powers, but that it will be dangerous. The biocomputers have been bonded to the team long enough to have completed the calculations for a portal back to their home planet, but that planet is plagued by war. They know that the Central Terminal should be able to increase their throughput, but for security purposes they were not programmed with the location of the terminal. They also won’t have access to their powers while on the planet, since the biocomputers will need to recover enough energy to get them home. The team agrees, and the biocomputers work together to open a portal to their home planet. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="On Synthax One, players can explore the area and have a few points of interest to discover. There are burned out farms, the remains of a recently fought battle, and a village. There is little to see on the farms. If the player goes to the battlefield, they are asked to help evacuate wounded to the local village. They can also speak with soldiers to learn more about the war the planet has been fighting with the villain and why Vince O'Ruin is trying to steal resources from these planets. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="In the village, players find clues to the location of the Central Terminal which leads them to a dangerous mountain. The team must fight several battles without access to their powers but eventually find the ruins that house the Central Terminal at the peak of the mountain. The biocomputers interface with the terminal and access increased processing power, which gives the team a new battle form and more powerful constructs.  "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="The players return to the portal where they arrived and make a vow to each other and their biocomputer partners to return when Earth is safe. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="Player Experience "/>
                <para Parent="Header 3"/>
                <Content Chars="On Synthax One, players are forced to play without their special abilities for the first time. This leaves them feeling vulnerable and anxious. As they explore, they will experience wonder and discovery as they see a fully alien world that is completely unlike Earth. Upon finding the information they need, players will be determined to get the new power despite their unpowered state. Once they have spoken to the Central Terminal, players will feel a sense of growth, not just from the power-up but from their new knowledge about the enemy. "/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PageObject>
        <PageObject XPosition="898.956521739132" YPosition="6357.91304347826" OwnPage="14" ItemID="248808655" ItemType="2" Width="238.086956521737" Height="238.086956521737" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="1" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="0.124003623188405" ImageScaleY="0.124003623188405" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="0" ImageRatio="1" ImagePageNumber="0" ImageFileName="Synthax One Map 2.png" ImageProfile="Embedded sRGB built-in" ImageColorimetricIntent="0" EmbeddedProfile="Embedded sRGB built-in" Path="M0 0 L238.087 0 L238.087 238.087 L0 238.087 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L238.087 0 L238.087 238.087 L0 238.087 L0 0 Z" gXpos="898.956521739132" gYpos="6357.91304347826" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1"/>
        <PageObject XPosition="140" YPosition="6716" OwnPage="15" ItemID="1256187971" ItemType="4" Width="532" Height="431.826086956524" FrameType="0" ClipEdited="0" LineWidth="1" LinePenStyle="1" ImageScaleX="1" ImageScaleY="1" ImageOffsetX="0" ImageOffsetY="0" ImageRotation="0" ImageVisible="1" ImageScaleType="1" ImageRatio="1" Columns="1" ColumnGap="0" AutomaticTextFrame="0" TextToFrameDistanceLeft="0" TextToFrameDistanceTop="0" TextToFrameDistanceBottom="0" TextToFrameDistanceRight="0" VerticalAlignment="0" FirstLineOffset="1" PathTextShowPath="0" PathTextDistanceFromPath="0" TextPathType="0" TextPathFlipped="0" Path="M0 0 L532 0 L532 431.826 L0 431.826 L0 0 Z" ContourLinePath="M0 0 L532 0 L532 431.826 L0 431.826 L0 0 Z" gXpos="140" gYpos="6716" gWidth="0" gHeight="0" Layer="0" NextItem="-1" BackItem="-1">
            <StoryText>
                <DefaultStyle/>
                <Content Chars="Resolution: The Observatory Showdown "/>
                <para Parent="Header 2"/>
                <Content Chars="The team has powered up just in time for Vince O'Ruin’s plans to enter their final stage. The team heads off to the observatory to put an end to the villainous plot to connect the worlds. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="On the road to the observatory is a cliffside quarry area (a traditional tokusatsu battle arena). Waiting to block the path is Zephir along with an army of mooks. The team battles Zephir, using their new battle forms to win. Rin has an emotional moment with Zephir immediately following the battle, which throws off the last bit of mind control that O'Ruin had over Zephir. Zephir is apologetic and ashamed but pushes past it to rejoin the team for the final conflict. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="The team enters the observatory and does battle with O'Ruin for the last time. It is a difficult battle, pushing each character to their limits. When the player finally defeats the boss, they shut down the process that would have connected the worlds. As they do so, they discover that a message was sent at the last moment, instructing Vince O'Ruin’s assistant to start “Operation Atlantis” on Synthax One. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="None of the team, including Zephir, know what Operation Atlantis is, but they know it must be trouble. The team prepares to return to Synthax One, knowing they won’t be returning to Earth for a long time, if at all. This serves as an open ending for the game as well as a setup for a potential sequel or DLC. "/>
                <para/>
                <Content Chars="Player Experience "/>
                <para Parent="Header 3"/>
                <Content Chars="As players begin the final level of the game, the determination they felt is still going strong. They have gotten more powerful and are feeling more confident in their abilities than ever. After defeating Zephir, they feel a moment of reconnection and wholeness that comes from reuniting as a team. Their battle with O’Ruin is hard-fought and will bring forward their mastery of their abilities and the game systems. The joy of victory follows, with the team celebrating their victory over the evil force. This lasts until the player discovers the message, which inspires a sense of anticipation and new purpose in them. "/>
                <trail/>
            </StoryText>
        </PageObject>
